// The same superstructure as `hauptbahn`, but with walls around it: `reverb`
// is how much the surroundings ring, 0 = open line, 1 = tunnel. The simulator
// mixes a reverb under everything the player hears and follows this value, so
// a line says where its tunnels are by assigning the type — nobody has to
// trace geometry at run time. A station hall or a deep cutting sits between
// the two, around 0.3 … 0.6.
(
    name: "Tunnel",
    color: (0.28, 0.27, 0.26),
    roughness: 1.0,
    reverb: 1.0,
    max_speed: 250.0,
    lzb: false,
)
